.TH CANDOR 1 "2026-11-15" "candor 0.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
candor \- command-line client for the Candor process monitor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B candor
[\fB\-\-socket\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B candor
shows what programs on the computer are doing, as seen by the
.BR candord (8)
daemon, and explains findings that look suspicious. It is a visibility tool
with explainable heuristics, not an antivirus.
.PP
It needs membership in the \fBcandor\fR group (or root) to connect.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Daemon version and kernel, available features (and why any is not), mode,
process counts, lost events.
.TP
.BR top " [" \-\-sort " cpu|mem|score] [" \-n " N]"
The process table.
.TP
.B tree
The process tree with tree scores.
.TP
.BR tail " [" \-\-proc " PID] [" \-\-count " N]"
Stream events live.
.TP
.BI detail " PID"
Files, connections, syscalls and findings of one process.
.BR \-\-maps
adds its memory map (own processes only, unless root).
.TP
.B findings
Every finding with its explanation and evidence.
.TP
.BI follow " PID" "\fR, \fBunfollow"
Trace only PID and its descendants, or go back to system-wide. Needs root or
the \fBcandor-act\fR group: while following, other processes are not traced.
.TP
.BR act " pause|resume|kill " \fIPID\fR
Experimental. Signal one process. The daemon must run with
\fB\-\-enable\-act\fR; needs root or \fBcandor-act\fR; protected processes
are refused.
.TP
.BR export " \-\-format json|csv [" \-\-raw "] [" \-\-redact\-ips ]
The current view. Personal details are redacted unless \fB\-\-raw\fR.
.TP
.BI replay " FILE"
Run a recording through the detector offline.
.TP
.BR "glasshouse run" " [" \-\-timeout " S] " \fIFILE\fR " [" \fIARGS\fR ]
Run FILE in the Glasshouse sandbox and print what it touched. Glasshouse is a
behaviour-demonstration sandbox, not a malware containment system; read the
warning it prints.
.TP
.BI "glasshouse report" " FILE.json"
Print a saved report.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable output.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Version, git commit and protocol version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 ok, 1 error, 2 usage, 3 daemon not running, 4 permission denied, 5 daemon error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR candor-gui (1),
.BR candord (8),
.BR candor-glasshouse (8),
/usr/share/doc/candor/README.md
